<title>FINLAND: FINNISH 2004 BOND YIELDS 5.55 PCT AT AUCTION.</title>
<headline>FINNISH 2004 BOND YIELDS 5.55 PCT AT AUCTION.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of the</p>
<p>S1/93 bond was announced by the State Treasury Office:</p>
<p> ISSUER:				 Republic of Finland</p>
<p> MATURITY:			     15-03-2004</p>
<p> COUPON:				 9.50 PCT</p>
<p> AUCTION YIELD:			5.55 PCT</p>
<p> PRICE:				  121.55</p>
<p> AUCTION AMOUNT			FIM 2,063 MLN</p>
<p> BID AMOUNT:			   FIM 3,113 MLN</p>
<p> PAYMENT FREQUENCY:		  YEARLY  NOTES:</p>
<p>The previous auction of the bond raised 1,992 million markka</p>
<p>at a price of 121.40 and a yield of 5.63 percent. After today's</p>
<p>auction, the outstanding amount is 47,835 million markka.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reutes.fi</p>
